# librispeech-mrm-wav2vec2

Multi-Resolution Masked Self-Supervised Speech Pretraining for Robust, Sample-Efficient ASR.

This repository implements:
- Data download + checksum verification for OpenSLR datasets (LibriSpeech SLR12, MUSAN SLR17, RIRS_NOISES SLR28).
- A supervised baseline: log-mel frontend + Conformer encoder + CTC + SpecAugment.
- An SSL baseline: wav2vec2-style pretraining with standard time-span masking only.
- The proposed MRM variant: time-span masking + feature-channel masking + a masking curriculum.
- Ablations (as in the plan):
  - Remove feature-channel masking (MRM -> time-span only) while keeping curriculum.
  - Remove curriculum (fixed mask prob/span from step 0) while keeping feature masking.
  - Robustness ablation: train/fine-tune without noise/RIR augmentation; evaluate on corrupted test sets.

Outputs:
- `artifacts/results.json` (machine-readable)
- `artifacts/report.md` (human report)

## Quick Start (Smoke)

The default `configs/smoke.yaml` uses a tiny synthetic dataset generated locally (no large downloads) and runs a fast end-to-end pipeline.

```bash
make all
```

Artifacts will be written to:
- `artifacts/results.json`
- `artifacts/report.md`
- `artifacts/runs/`

## Full Data (OpenSLR)

The full plan uses LibriSpeech + MUSAN + RIRS_NOISES.

1. Create the environment:

```bash
# CPU wheels (default)
make setup

# For CUDA wheels, set a PyTorch wheel index URL. Example (CUDA 12.1):
PIP_EXTRA_INDEX_URL=https://download.pytorch.org/whl/cu121 make setup
```

2. Download + verify + extract (sequential, per OpenSLR guidance):

```bash
.venv/bin/python -m librispeech_mrm.cli --config configs/full.yaml data
```

## Reproducibility

- Global seed is set via config.
- `torch.backends.cudnn.deterministic` and deterministic algorithms can be enabled (slower) via config.
- Dataloader worker seeds are derived deterministically.

## Command Line

All tasks are accessible from one entrypoint:

```bash
.venv/bin/python -m librispeech_mrm.cli --help
.venv/bin/python -m librispeech_mrm.cli --config configs/smoke.yaml data
.venv/bin/python -m librispeech_mrm.cli --config configs/smoke.yaml train
.venv/bin/python -m librispeech_mrm.cli --config configs/smoke.yaml eval
.venv/bin/python -m librispeech_mrm.cli --config configs/smoke.yaml report
```

## Notes

- The smoke config is meant to validate wiring quickly.
- The full experiments (460h+ SSL pretraining) are compute-heavy; use `configs/full.yaml` and adjust batch sizes, `torchrun` settings, and logging to your cluster.
